.SH "NAME"
aerospace-focus-back-and-forth \- Switch between the current and previously focused elements back and forth
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
aerospace focus\-back\-and\-forth [\-h|\-\-help]
.fi
.br
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Switch between the current and previously focused elements back and forth.
The element is either a window or an empty workspace.
.sp
AeroSpace stores only one previously focused window in history,
which means that if you close the previous window,
\f(CRfocus\-back\-and\-forth\fP has no window to switch focus to.
In that case, the command will exit with non\-zero exit code.
.sp
That\(cqs why it may be preferred to combine \f(CRfocus\-back\-and\-forth\fP with \f(CRworkspace\-back\-and\-forth\fP:
.br
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
aerospace focus\-back\-and\-forth || aerospace workspace\-back\-and\-forth
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
Also see: workspace\-back\-and\-forth
.SH "OPTIONS"
.sp
\-h, \-\-help
.RS 4
Print help
.RE
